WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.025 --> 00:00:01.411
- Everyone's a critic.

00:00:01.411 --> 00:00:03.660
But for our episode on music criticism,

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.560
we chose to focus on YouTube music critic,

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:07.450
Anthony Fantano's The Needle Drop.

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:08.283
- Bam!

00:00:08.283 --> 00:00:10.717
Hey everyone, Anthony Fantano here.

00:00:10.717 --> 00:00:13.170
The internet's busiest music nerd.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:15.680
- One, because his scoring
system makes it crystal clear

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.270
what he considers better or worse music.

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:20.577
And two, because one of
our producers is a huge fan

00:00:20.577 --> 00:00:23.602
and gets really upset when he
gives Young Thug low scores.

00:00:23.602 --> 00:00:26.250
- I'm feeling a strong four
to a light five on this thing.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.610
- So we want to unlock the code

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:29.430
of how to get a good rating from Anthony

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:32.530
so that we can create our own
Needle Drop approved song.

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:34.250
- Lenarae and I are gonna produce a track

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:36.810
with the help of Anthony Fantano.

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:39.595
- We're trying to find a
track that you can join us on.

00:00:39.595 --> 00:00:40.975
- Cool.

00:00:40.975 --> 00:00:44.050
(distorted audio buzzing)

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:48.130
- What do you feel like the
purpose of music critics is?

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:52.073
- I think it's more of
a service of curation

00:00:52.073 --> 00:00:54.310
and allowing the audience to know

00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:56.840
in this very saturated field of music,

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:58.650
this is stuff that I
think is worth your time.

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:00.170
- How important do you feel it is

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:02.760
for critics to actually be musicians?

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.600
- I don't know if it's super essential.

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:07.040
Because I know there are a lot
of super successful critics

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:09.720
whose opinions that I think over the years

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:10.729
have proven to be super valid,

00:01:10.729 --> 00:01:13.330
who haven't necessarily prided themselves

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:15.270
as being musicians.

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:19.080
I think that there are
certainly aspects of music

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:21.569
and music production
that maybe as a critic

00:01:21.569 --> 00:01:26.569
you should do your due
diligence to try to understand,

00:01:26.677 --> 00:01:29.370
to at least be able to comment on.

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:31.400
And giving that I'm reviewing records,

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.236
understanding and knowing production,

00:01:33.236 --> 00:01:36.360
or at least the basics of
it, that's kind of essential

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.950
because that is literally the
process of making the album.

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:39.783
- That's how I think.

00:01:39.783 --> 00:01:42.754
- Since 2009, he's
released over 3,000 videos

00:01:42.754 --> 00:01:44.140
on The Needle Drop

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:47.139
as well as on his other
channel, simply called Fantano.

00:01:47.139 --> 00:01:49.270
And he's developed a rating scale

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:51.250
that goes from zero to ten,

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:52.907
with qualifiers such as...

00:01:52.907 --> 00:01:54.720
- Feeling a light to decent six.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:56.300
Feeling a decent to a strong eight.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.133
It's not good.

00:01:57.133 --> 00:01:57.966
(explosion)

00:01:57.966 --> 00:01:59.580
- He's only ever given
a ten out of ten rating

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:00.468
to these five albums.

00:02:00.468 --> 00:02:01.301
♪ Get get get get ♪

00:02:01.301 --> 00:02:02.134
♪ Got got got got ♪

00:02:02.134 --> 00:02:02.967
♪ Blood rush to my ♪

00:02:02.967 --> 00:02:03.800
♪ Head lit hot lock ♪

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:06.715
♪ (Vocalizing) ♪

00:02:06.715 --> 00:02:08.134
♪ I love myself ♪

00:02:08.134 --> 00:02:10.564
♪ The world is a ghetto with
big guns and picket signs ♪

00:02:10.564 --> 00:02:12.409
♪ Moving forward ♪

00:02:12.409 --> 00:02:14.445
♪ Keep moving forward ♪

00:02:14.445 --> 00:02:16.996
♪ Breezes into the driveway
and kills the engine ♪

00:02:16.996 --> 00:02:17.910
♪ Sits for a spell ♪

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:19.700
- He did give a ten to the album

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:22.520
Pink Flag by Wire in a
special classic review,

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:24.610
but since then the
video's been taken down,

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:25.889
so we'll just leave it out for now.

00:02:25.889 --> 00:02:28.120
- And for a counterpoint,
we also looked up

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:31.413
the two albums to receive
a zero out of ten.

00:02:31.413 --> 00:02:33.220
♪ Seems I hate him too ♪

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:35.588
♪ Seems my collar's blue ♪

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:36.450
♪ And my lawyer say it's urgent ♪

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:37.919
♪ I'ma call him in an hour ♪

00:02:37.919 --> 00:02:40.154
- So how does a piece of music
get a perfect 10 out of 10

00:02:40.154 --> 00:02:42.847
rating, and avoid the 0 out of 10?

00:02:42.847 --> 00:02:46.450
Fantano is the first to call
his own criticism subjective.

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:48.030
- Even though I try to
explicitly tell people

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:50.510
over, and over, and over,
this is just my opinion,

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:51.520
its not doctrine.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:54.110
Just like, please like, you
know form your own opinion,

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:56.420
disagree with me all you
want, I'm not hating on you

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:57.253
for disagreeing on me.

00:02:57.253 --> 00:03:01.910
- After doing this for a decade,
have you given any ratings

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:04.520
to an album that you'd like
to change in retrospect?

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:06.750
- Nothing like super crazy,

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:09.240
I once hated, and I thought it was garbage

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:10.300
- Just love it
- and now its amazing now.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:11.300
- All right, okay.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.393
So that's it, video's over right?

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:15.690
Just do your best and
hope he likes your music?

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:18.850
Well not exactly, we did
find 7 key elements that all

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:20.480
of his 10 out of 10 albums shared.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:23.521
- I'm lovin' this record,
freakin' lovin' this record.

00:03:23.521 --> 00:03:26.184
And it just happens to be
fantastically enjoyable.

00:03:26.184 --> 00:03:29.630
- And 7 key elements that his
0 out of 10 albums lacked.

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:32.453
- No and I'm, I'm not interested in that.

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:36.090
- Our first tip is to go big or go home.

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:38.700
One aspect that will get you
into Fantano's good graces

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:40.280
is to make your music epic.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:41.690
- And grand and rich.

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:43.900
So dense, lengthy.

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:46.800
Color, the volume, the
texture, its all on high.

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:49.080
This whole new record is
an undertaking in length.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:51.460
What's grown into a 30-story monster.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.300
Its two hours long!

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:56.320
- All that said, don't think
just making your music longer

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:58.930
and louder is an automatic
ticket to a higher score.

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:01.060
- I do love loud music, its important to

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:01.910
have dynamics though.

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:03.440
- Contrast, okay
- You know because

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:06.241
Loud is not significant
if you don't have soft.

00:04:06.241 --> 00:04:09.140
- Our second is probably the most obvious.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:11.510
If you want a perfect
score; don't be sloppy.

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:13.330
- This album is a pile of slop.

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:15.550
They're so weak, they're
so badly performed.

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:19.277
Terrible singing, terrible
bars, flat production.

00:04:19.277 --> 00:04:22.260
- Cultivate the skills
in order to be precise,

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:24.133
crisp, and meticulous.

00:04:24.133 --> 00:04:25.630
- Tons of precision.

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:28.660
So crisp, they sound so
fantastic, they sound so clear.

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:31.150
So meticulously placed together.

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:34.723
(upbeat rock music)

00:04:34.723 --> 00:04:37.150
- Of course we don't want
to say that there isn't any

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:39.556
artistry or enjoyment in sloppy music.

00:04:39.556 --> 00:04:42.024
Not everyone has to be a virtuoso.

00:04:42.024 --> 00:04:45.780
But if you're putting out sloppy
and poorly executed music,

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:48.318
you probably weren't going
for that 10 out of 10

00:04:48.318 --> 00:04:50.110
perfect score anyway.

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:52.060
- Maybe the most striking
point uncovered in the making

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:54.555
of this video, was that
Kid Cudi received a rare

00:04:54.555 --> 00:04:56.067
0 out of 10 rating.

00:04:56.067 --> 00:04:59.280
But then 2 albums later,
received a 10 out of 10 rating.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:01.120
Could the low expectations from the first

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:03.109
0 out of 10 record have lead
to the perfect score with

00:05:03.109 --> 00:05:04.980
Kid's See Ghosts?

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:06.745
Fantano does use a lot of
language that expresses his

00:05:06.745 --> 00:05:08.790
appreciation of progress.

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:10.932
- I was left after this
album wondering "Where could

00:05:10.932 --> 00:05:13.400
Kendrick go after this."

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:16.060
He has gone through this
artistic metamorphosis.

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:19.060
Since that album was released
I think they've done, a

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:21.680
great job of improving
upon that formula as well.

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:25.050
Also sounds completely unlike
anything Kanye has dropped

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.716
so far this year, really dropped ever.

00:05:27.716 --> 00:05:28.861
(eerie vocal reversed)

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:31.183
♪ It feels so good it should cost ♪

00:05:31.183 --> 00:05:34.477
- And by contrast his frustration
with the lack of progress.

00:05:34.477 --> 00:05:36.520
- Its like its gotten worse than ever.

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:39.704
Progress is good, its,
its not always necessary.

00:05:39.704 --> 00:05:42.300
I would say the Daughter's
record is a bit of an

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:43.133
example of that.

00:05:43.133 --> 00:05:44.836
Because the thing is like, they
had almost a 10 year hiatus

00:05:44.836 --> 00:05:46.084
between those 2 records.

00:05:46.084 --> 00:05:50.270
And certainly I agree that the,
the newest record is better.

00:05:50.270 --> 00:05:52.900
I wasn't really like "Oh man
is this one gonna live up to

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:53.733
the last one?"

00:05:53.733 --> 00:05:55.153
You know the last one was pretty decent.

00:05:55.153 --> 00:05:58.200
- The fourth thing you need to
know about 10 out of 10 music

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.600
is that Fantano likes his music to be.

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:02.830
- Just beautifully cohesive.

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:05.160
Seamless, they move so fluidly.

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:07.777
Its always consistent,
its present, its on point.

00:06:07.777 --> 00:06:11.027
(energetic rock music)

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:14.430
If you want your listener
to become truly immersed

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:16.250
into your entire piece.

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:19.200
You have to try your very best
to make sure your music has.

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:22.180
- Some kind of common
thread running through them.

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:25.000
- It was seen, another thing
that Fantano gives high ratings

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:26.780
to is music that is troubled.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:28.760
- Tortured and demented sounds.

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:30.290
Sickening murder scene.

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:31.123
Insane.

00:06:31.123 --> 00:06:33.274
Emotional and mental problems.

00:06:33.274 --> 00:06:35.020
Unsettling, disturbing.

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:36.706
♪ Let me off, screeching halt, ♪

00:06:36.706 --> 00:06:38.225
♪ Concussion blinding, not my fault ♪

00:06:38.225 --> 00:06:41.050
- Does this taste for dark
music give us insight into

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:42.803
Fantano's character specifically?

00:06:42.803 --> 00:06:44.590
Or might it indicate something about

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:46.050
10 out of 10 music itself?

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:47.360
Billboard recently published a

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:50.097
study saying that 73 percent
of independent musicians,

00:06:50.097 --> 00:06:52.049
report symptoms of mental illness.

00:06:52.049 --> 00:06:54.670
So either we have to be
brave enough to make art with

00:06:54.670 --> 00:06:58.156
our inner darkness, or, those
of us with darkness inside

00:06:58.156 --> 00:07:01.197
are statistically more likely
to create the kind of troubled

00:07:01.197 --> 00:07:03.940
music critics like Fantano value.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:05.960
- I was looking back at like
some of the records that I put

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:07.400
in my top 10.

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:10.260
And some of the records I
gave 10's to, I was like "Man,

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:12.480
why are these albums
(expletive) depressing?"

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:14.940
And then recently somebody
made a meme where the golden

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:17.930
retriever said "Anthony Fantano,"
and then the giant scary

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:20.365
beast said "music Anthony Fantano likes."

00:07:20.365 --> 00:07:23.600
I mean I don't personally
buy into the notion, which I

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:25.240
think is kind of overplayed in a lot of

00:07:25.240 --> 00:07:26.310
music writng circles.

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:27.143
That like,

00:07:27.143 --> 00:07:27.976
(Hands clap)

00:07:27.976 --> 00:07:32.169
sad art is the best, its
all about sad art dude.

00:07:32.169 --> 00:07:34.730
(expletive) That,
(expletive) that happy art.

00:07:34.730 --> 00:07:36.080
And also I'm sorry am I swearing

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:37.528
too much for PBS, I don't know?

00:07:37.528 --> 00:07:39.351
I think there's some really
great records that I love and

00:07:39.351 --> 00:07:41.820
that I've supported over the
years that have, you know some

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:46.520
like supremely, bouncy, bright,
colorful qualities to them.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:48.720
- Music critics love
listening to music so give

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:51.980
them something that they really
have to actively listen to.

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:54.365
For Fantano, it seems
that 10 out of 10 music

00:07:54.365 --> 00:07:55.750
demands you to be.

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:59.510
- Tied to your chair and
your, eyelids are peeled back.

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:00.760
- It demands attention.

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:04.127
- Songs on here do require
quite a bit of attention.

00:08:04.127 --> 00:08:06.221
♪ 40 acres and a mule?
A piano, a guitar? ♪

00:08:06.221 --> 00:08:07.923
♪ Anything, see my name is Lucy ♪

00:08:07.923 --> 00:08:10.560
- This is essential, if you
want them to give you their

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:13.550
highest level of attention,
you've got to infuse your

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:17.170
music with nuance, detail, and variety.

00:08:17.170 --> 00:08:20.034
- The record is a fantastic nuanced and

00:08:20.034 --> 00:08:22.930
very detailed character portrayal.

00:08:22.930 --> 00:08:25.018
In short, don't make background music.

00:08:25.018 --> 00:08:28.230
I do agree with this, but I
would attribute a lot of it

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:30.280
to like a reviewers bias.

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:32.340
Because I'm listening to
the record in a way that

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:34.868
your average casual listener might not be.

00:08:34.868 --> 00:08:37.520
- No amount of complexity
is going to save you if

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:39.130
you're not being genuine.

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:41.650
- Well it doesn't feel like
a genuine expression of love.

00:08:41.650 --> 00:08:44.280
- Be free with yourself,
be free with your music.

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:46.070
- Throwing out this idea of freedom.

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:46.903
- Be open.

00:08:46.903 --> 00:08:50.130
- This world is opening up!

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:51.738
- Get face-to-face with your listener.

00:08:51.738 --> 00:08:54.165
- Pop, being just so in your face.

00:08:54.165 --> 00:08:57.270
- And above all, do it unapologetically.

00:08:57.270 --> 00:09:00.510
- This really trashy,
unapologetic character

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:03.610
that MC ride depicts.

00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:06.310
- Its funny, but while making
this video we came across an

00:09:06.310 --> 00:09:09.660
amusing Reddit conspiracy that
Fantano only gives positive

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:12.034
reviews to artists who go
shirtless at some point.

00:09:12.034 --> 00:09:14.934
It's a ridiculous conspiracy,
but whether or not showing

00:09:14.934 --> 00:09:18.160
your critics your skin gets
you higher marks, opening up

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:20.620
and showing your vulnerable
side will be rewarded.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:21.453
- I agree.

00:09:21.453 --> 00:09:23.910
- So, no barriers.

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:24.870
Just connect.

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:29.690
- I do love a feeling of a
record that is, authentic.

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:31.770
That feels kind of raw emotionally.

00:09:31.770 --> 00:09:36.209
That is delivering some kind
of intense emotion to you.

00:09:36.209 --> 00:09:37.229
- Mm-hmm
- It doesn't have to be like

00:09:37.229 --> 00:09:40.670
anger, it doesn't have to be
sadness, it can be an intense

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:42.043
sense of happiness as well.

00:09:42.043 --> 00:09:45.030
- Sometimes artists get rubbed
the wrong way when they get

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:46.160
a negative review.

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:49.020
We just want to point out that
from what we've seen, Anthony

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:51.740
genuinely wants the music
that he's listening to,

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:52.573
to be good.

00:09:52.573 --> 00:09:54.940
He's often rooting for the artist.

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:56.360
- I wish it didn't hurt feelings.

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:58.110
I wish it didn't create negativity.

00:09:58.110 --> 00:10:00.282
I wish it didn't, but I
don't know what to do,

00:10:00.282 --> 00:10:01.850
I don't know what to do.

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:03.870
If you put yourself out there
in any way, you're a vlogger,

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:05.751
you're a reviewer, you're a musician,

00:10:05.751 --> 00:10:08.930
you're this, you're that,
you're going to catch criticism.

00:10:08.930 --> 00:10:10.411
People are going to say
negative things about you.

00:10:10.411 --> 00:10:13.280
I've had horrible things said
about me over the years that

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:14.113
I have been doing this.

00:10:14.113 --> 00:10:17.237
In my view, especially
since I do my best not to

00:10:17.237 --> 00:10:20.958
make anything in my reviews on
a level of a personal attack.

00:10:20.958 --> 00:10:23.970
I feel like in the grander
scheme of things, you could get

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:25.750
worse stuff than a review.

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:29.020
- Do you know many or
some of the artists that

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:30.720
you've reviewed personally?

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:33.300
- I've met some and have had
some acquaintanceships with

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:35.810
them, but I try not to, get to close for

00:10:35.810 --> 00:10:36.920
professional reasons.

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:40.460
- Or does it help that you
don't know them to be free

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:43.950
to criticize as harshly as you want?

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:46.900
- I try to prevent myself from
going to that point where I

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:49.270
know them in such a way where
it would be difficult to

00:10:49.270 --> 00:10:51.770
critique there music in
an open and an honest way.

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:55.300
Because openly at the end
of the day what my channel

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:56.300
is for my fans.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:58.929
- So even if you do get a bad
review, its likely that some

00:10:58.929 --> 00:11:02.020
critics just don't like
your kind of music.

00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:04.850
So the best thing to do, is
to get out there and find an

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:06.502
audience that does.

00:11:06.502 --> 00:11:11.000
So I have a question, what if
you provided us with maybe one

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:12.597
of your ideal grooves

00:11:12.597 --> 00:11:14.590
- On a baseline?
- That you play?

00:11:14.590 --> 00:11:17.456
Yeah, and then we can,
we can go from there.

00:11:17.456 --> 00:11:20.270
- That could potentially
work, I can work with a

00:11:20.270 --> 00:11:21.150
drum beat as well.

00:11:21.150 --> 00:11:23.110
- I can send you the drums I did.

00:11:23.110 --> 00:11:23.943
- Yeah why don't

00:11:23.943 --> 00:11:24.776
- Yeah!
- Instead of it going

00:11:24.776 --> 00:11:28.740
from LA, me, Anthony, we
can go LA, Anthony, me.

00:11:28.740 --> 00:11:29.641
- Boom.
- Yeah exactly, because then

00:11:29.641 --> 00:11:31.107
you've laid down the rhythm
section essentially and then

00:11:31.107 --> 00:11:33.532
you can just do whatever
you want on top of that.

00:11:33.532 --> 00:11:37.390
- We think its just so
interesting if we could see, you

00:11:37.390 --> 00:11:39.410
contributing to a track that,

00:11:39.410 --> 00:11:41.790
maybe the audience can then review

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:42.960
that amongst themselves.

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:46.090
But just to, flip the script a little bit.

00:11:46.090 --> 00:11:48.068
- We're trying to make
a 10 out of 10 right?

00:11:48.068 --> 00:11:51.068
(gentle jazz music)

00:12:12.488 --> 00:12:15.488
(upbeat jazz music)

00:12:59.927 --> 00:13:02.030
- What did you think of our song?

00:13:02.030 --> 00:13:03.022
Did you love it?

00:13:03.022 --> 00:13:04.036
Did you hate it?

00:13:04.036 --> 00:13:05.400
What would you rate it?

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:08.223
And if you like our show,
please subscribe to see more

00:13:08.223 --> 00:13:11.582
episodes where LA and I
travel across the country.

00:13:11.582 --> 00:13:14.327
(gentle audio reverse)

